course: dictionary
lesson: 9801
title: Suture: stitches and seams
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. «The doctor used a suture to close the cut on his knee.» Doctors close cuts with stitches, so here a suture is a stitch.
explain: «The skull is 22 bones fitted together with zigzag seams called sutures.» Bones are not closed with stitches, so this suture must be a seam, a fixed joint where two bones meet.
explain: Suture can also be a verb. To suture a wound is to sew it closed. Ask yourself: is the word a thing or an action? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: A suture is a stitch, or a row of stitches, that closes a cut or wound.
fact: To suture a wound means to sew it closed.
fact: A suture is also a fixed, wiggly joint between bones, like the lines where the bones of the skull meet.
fact: «The skull has 22 bones: 8 around the brain and 14 in the face, joined by zigzag seams called sutures.»
fact: In a baby the sutures are still open, with soft spots between the bones, so the head can squeeze through at birth.
exercise: «The doctor used a suture to close the cut.» What is a suture here? | A bone in the face | *A stitch | A soft spot on a baby's head | A kind of bandage
exercise: «The sutures in the skull are zigzag seams.» What does suture mean here? | A sharp needle | A stitch in a cut | A loud crack of thunder | *A fixed, wiggly joint between bones
exercise: Ella says, «The nurse will suture the cut.» What is the nurse going to do? | Cover it with a plaster and nothing else | Cut the skin open wider | Wash the wound with hot water | *Sew the cut closed
test: Why are a baby's sutures still open at birth? | So the baby can hear better | *So the head can squeeze through and the brain can grow | Because the baby has no bones yet | So the skull can get heavier
test: «Some sutures dissolve on their own, but others must be removed after about a week.» What does dissolve mean here? | *Melt away by themselves | Get bigger and stronger | Be cut off with scissors | Stay in place forever
exam: «The skull looks like one big bone, but it is 22 bones fitted together with zigzag seams called sutures.» What does this tell you a suture is? | A bandage for a wound | *A zigzag seam between bones | A tool doctors use to cut the skin | A soft spot that closes slowly
